HONEST CHARACTERIZATION: this is a re-quantization WORKAROUND. It moves the via to a
grid row where the gap is legal rather than teaching the router why the gap was there.
The underlying source-level gap remains: route_nets.py cannot see a same-net
spacing conflict at all. A durable fix belongs in route_nets.py -- either make
via_pad_cells() honour min-spacing against the net's OWN landing stub, or snap the
first via off a port-landing node to a row at least (pad/2 + stub/2 + min_space) away.
Flagged to the orchestrator as a source fix, not re-attempted here.

